From ec4cc1aa7ea92125a88a123dba7189f8759645db Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Van Tran <tetcu@fgorg.vn>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 15:55:15 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] feat(boards): lanes, parent chips, status age, child panel
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

- feat(issues): show a sub-issue's parent on board cards and list rows

  A chip with the parent's identifier and title (tooltip: Sub-issue of …) next
  to the identifier, so children are told apart from top-level issues at a
  glance. Parents keep their sub-issue progress ring.

- feat(issues): when each open issue entered its status

  GET /api/issues/status-since[?project_id=] lists, for every issue not done or
  cancelled, its status and when it entered it (last status_changed activity,
  else creation). Core @multica/core/board-gates: the query, daysInColumn, and
  gateStatuses (steps a person approves). Reference: Jira's days in column.

- feat(issues): child issues by status and days in status

  The sub-issue panel shows a bar of the children by status next to the done
  count, and each open child shows how many days it has sat in its status (from
  one day, red from five). Reference: Jira's Child issues panel.

- feat(boards): lanes for a board of several workflows

  A board that shows issues of several workflows — a project whose Type rules use
  another workflow, or the workspace board when the workspace has more than one
  workflow — shows four columns that each hold several statuses: To do, In
  progress, Awaiting approval (every step a person approves, locked heading,
  longest wait first) and Done. Cards name their real status and goal, and every
  card shows its days in column (from one day, red from five). Dropping on a lane
  picks the lane's first status the card's own workflow (its Type rule's) allows.
  The workspace board loads the steps of every workflow. A board of one workflow
  keeps one column per step.
  Reference: Jira board column mapping, days in column.

Patch-Id: boards
